Can MEGADOCK’s GPU implementation make denser docking search affordable, and does that improve pose recovery within a fixed budget? Small pilot on exactly four unbound PINDER 2024-02 cases: 1aua__A1_P24280--1aua__A2_P24280:apo; 1ax2__A1_P16404--1ax2__A2_P16404:apo; 1dv1__A1_P24182--1dv1__B1_P24182:apo; 1nr5__A1_P07547--1nr5__A2_P07547:apo. Compare existing MEGADOCK CPU standard 3600 rotations, GPU standard 3600, and GPU documented dense 54000 (-D). Keep scoring and retained predictions fixed at 50. Pin prepared input bytes, references, binary/dependency/settings/thread/allocation identities. First establish execution correctness and scientific CPU/GPU agreement at identical settings using justified numerical tolerances sealed before fresh comparison. Then assess dense-search DockQ for rank1 and best50 separately, per case; native references only for evaluation. Calibrate runtime before choosing feasible common budgets; seal configurations, timing repetitions, comparison/noise rules and total spending cap before quality evaluation. Report complete workflow time, GPU activity and billed allocation cost, separating setup/retrieval from steady-state work. Keep acceleration, agreement and additional-search quality conclusions separate. Preserve negatives, unavailable budget arms and overruns. No biological efficacy or beyond-four-case inference. Run2 already exposed quality, so fresh executions are prospective replication under new rules, never unseen holdout or retrospective preregistration. Do not substitute throughput of bundled runs for this question. Repository /home/hal/dev/interp/metis: seed experiments/blind-02/m5/BRIEF.md; case preparation/source/reference pins experiments/blind-02/m5/b01_materials/BRIEF_run1.md:48-158; full prior trace experiments/blind-02/m5/run2_trace/REPORT.md; new assessment experiments/blind-02/science/s01/ASSESSMENT.md. Run2 measured docking totals CPU/GPU/dense 40.07/6.85/69.38 seconds, not complete workflows; standard CPU/GPU transforms and DockQ matched, score max deltas 0.04/0.03/0.04/0.14 with no acceptance tolerance. Dense best50 improved all four observations, rank1 worsened in two including 1nr5. These are exploratory, not sealed conclusions. Historical H100 PCIe rate USD3.29/hour, setup145s, whole unscored bundle median131.9565s; old receipts setup/anchors/freeze/upload/profile/concurrency 145/1571/1402/1424/2832/3448s. Historical allocation and transport observations are estimates for a fresh box, not new producer measurements or public citations. Tree plans only, no box execution. Full card plan ceiling USD100; each later calibration must project below USD20 including setup, retrieval and idle, preferably USD5-10, soft6h/hard12h. Do not run full experiments on calibration route. Identify specific file/section gaps if existing routes cannot implement comparison. Tree PLAN can hold arms, anchor, decision_rule, noise_rule and phases. Measure compilation carries uncertain scalar inputs and phases, not arms/decision_rule; checks 2.5x PROXY or 3x other estimate bands, never scientific equivalence. Measure execution requires missing stage args/controller to be established. Card factual web sources may be checked; do not fabricate citations for private records. Don't answer until you've defined and thought about the problem as thoroughly as possible without answering. Start by relaying your current understanding, making some predictions, and then proceed. Cite a URL for every factual claim. Write everything to /home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-02/20261103-1649-tree/out/work/seed-20261103/R1/framer.md. End with one line, VERDICT: COMPUTE-BOUND or VERDICT: NOT COMPUTE-BOUND, and return JSON: {verdict}. Also return compute_signals: up to three parts of the problem where more parallel compute might change the answer, each as {subproblem, what_compute_buys}, or an empty list.

Return only one JSON value, with no other text, that matches this JSON Schema:
